/// Establish a subtree in which widgets can opt into persisting states after
/// being destroyed.
/// <code>PageStorage</code> is used to save and restore values that can outlive the widget.
/// For example, when multiple pages are grouped in tabs, when a page is
/// switched out, its widget is destroyed and its state is lost. By adding a
/// <code>PageStorage</code> at the root and adding a <code>PageStorageKey</code> to each page, some of the
/// page’s state (e.g. the scroll position of a <code>Scrollable</code> widget) will be stored
/// automatically in its closest ancestor <code>PageStorage</code>, and restored when it’s
